<!-- @before Internal Mechanics :: guide -->
### A clock comparison detects; it does not choose

Compare every component. A version dominates another only when it is at least as large everywhere and strictly larger somewhere. If neither dominates, the application needs siblings or a merge policy. Advancing B’s process clock must not relabel an old write as a new one. [Dynamo’s version reconciliation](https://www.allthingsdistributed.com/files/amazon-dynamo-sosp2007.pdf).

<!-- @before Staff Engineer Thinking :: staff -->
### Retirement changes what the clock can prove

Stable actor identity and retained history are correctness inputs. A pruning budget must not turn an old offline version into an apparently new write; define retirement or reset before removing causal information.
